{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.6a690b5691","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-398","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Tunnel is in southern Norway. It opened in 1913.</li><li>Its length is 22 kilometers.</li><li>The Brookhaven Tunnel is in southern Brazil. It opened in 1974.</li><li>Its length is 14 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Glenrock Tunnel is in southern Norway, and the Brookhaven Tunnel is in southern Brazil.","The length of the Glenrock Tunnel (22 kilometers) is greater than that of the Brookhaven Tunnel (14 kilometers).","The Glenrock Tunnel, which is in southern Norway, is one of several tunnels that pass under a mountain range.","The Glenrock Tunnel opened in 1913, while the Brookhaven Tunnel opened in 1974."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b3788dcf4e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-2","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Rahman is a marine biologist.</li><li>Rahman wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Rahman recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Rahman found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Rahman concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Rahman recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.","Rahman concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","Because whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often, Rahman concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","Rahman found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.11bf4168f1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-3","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Moreau is a marine biologist.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Moreau recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Moreau found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Moreau concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often, Moreau concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","Moreau found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","Moreau concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","To investigate the question, Moreau recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.02e0cfee2e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-5","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Omar Duarte is a marine biologist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Duarte recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Duarte found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Duarte concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Duarte concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","To investigate the question, Duarte recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.","Duarte found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","Because whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often, Duarte concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.335a56b428","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-9","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Rahman is an ecologist.</li><li>Rahman wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Rahman compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Rahman found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Rahman concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Rahman compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.","Because robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier, Rahman concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","Rahman found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Rahman concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.5dd9973ca6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-16","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Haddad is a psychologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Haddad had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Haddad found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Haddad concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Haddad found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.","Haddad concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","To investigate the question, Haddad had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Because students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly, Haddad concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.a9b2a24eb5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-20","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Nakamura is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Nakamura grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Nakamura found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Nakamura grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Nakamura found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Because fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer, Nakamura concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.2a92d96ee1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-33","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Solberg is an entomologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Because bees visited the blue feeders most often, Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","To investigate the question, Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.48721d4b87","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-63","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Maren Brennan is an astronomer.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Brennan measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Brennan found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Brennan concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Brennan measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.","Because the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days, Brennan concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","Brennan concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","Brennan found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.a70eac990f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-75","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Varga is an economist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Varga tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Varga found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Varga concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","To investigate the question, Varga tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Because output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly, Varga concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Varga found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b33459ab51","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-77","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Duarte is an economist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Duarte tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Duarte found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Duarte concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly, Duarte concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Duarte concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","To investigate the question, Duarte tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Duarte found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.82f5a208d4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-87","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kwame Mensah is an urban planner.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Mensah measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Mensah found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler, Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Mensah found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","To investigate the question, Mensah measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.c63b9546d7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-110","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Mensah is a primatologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Mensah observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Mensah found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier, Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","Mensah found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","To investigate the question, Mensah observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.0c4479fb91","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-120","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Vance is an ornithologist.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Vance measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Vance found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Vance concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Vance found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Vance concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","To investigate the question, Vance measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Because species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings, Vance concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.8f0267338c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-121","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Ferreira is an ornithologist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Because species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings, Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."}
